WEBVTT

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:04.980
Inconceivable.

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:08.390
Why, when it's summer break, 
are we going to school?

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:11.860
It's attendance day.

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:15.010
Why does such a thing 
exist in the first place?

00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:17.740
Quit complaining and get ready.

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:24.120
Thank you for coming to morning 
practice before school.

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:29.000
I thought, since it's attendance day, 
we might want to put off practice.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:29.800
No!

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:33.830
I want to improve more.

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:36.020
So let's practice more.

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:45.600
Guys, let's get going.

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:48.260
Zomi-tan, carry me.

00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:49.940
There you are.

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:37.200
Aigae-san... You were a grade-schooler?

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:38.500
Hey!

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:40.090
<i>That's</i> what you're shocked about?

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:42.090
<b>Shiromidai Elementary School
Class 5-2
Ogi Koume</b>

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:42.090
Ogi Koume?

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:45.180
I never thought you'd 
have such a boring name.

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:47.260
Sounds like a grandma.

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:49.600
Wh-Who are you calling a loli granny?!

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:54.440
There was a meeting on the island, 
right after you guys left.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:58.440
They decided to end the 
Kiryu priestess tradition.

00:02:59.850 --> 00:03:05.580
I drew up a quick ink wash 
painting to take my place.

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:09.210
Pretending I gave it about fifty 
years' worth of god powers.

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:10.830
"Pretending"?

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:15.620
So to make up for everything up until now, 
they're granting me all my wishes.

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:19.290
So I asked them to let me 
live on the main island.

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:20.840
Along with Aigae-san?

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:24.350
I'm Kiryu-sama's assistant, so of course.

00:03:25.670 --> 00:03:28.500
Living in the city with Kiryu-sama...

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:30.070
It's like a dream.

00:03:30.070 --> 00:03:32.840
So getting down to business...

00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:35.670
Now that I'm free...

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:40.880
Hibiki, let's...

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:42.530
get married.

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:49.190
My mom asked you to take care of me going 
forward, and you said "okay," right?

00:03:49.190 --> 00:03:50.870
So it's settled, we're getting married.

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:54.130
M-M-M-M-Married?!

00:03:54.130 --> 00:03:56.510
Don't panic, Sakura.

00:03:56.510 --> 00:04:00.320
You can't get married simply by 
being hyped up about it by yourself.

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:03.260
You also need...

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:06.350
Something irreversible.

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:08.170
That's right, something irreversible.

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:11.270
Wait, what's that again, Sakura?

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:13.130
W-Well...

00:04:13.130 --> 00:04:14.940
A k-kiss, I guess?

00:04:15.910 --> 00:04:17.220
That's it, a kiss.

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:18.530
Got it.

00:04:18.530 --> 00:04:20.280
Let's kiss, Kyo-san.

00:04:20.870 --> 00:04:22.330
Wait, wait.

00:04:22.330 --> 00:04:23.780
Calm down, everyone.

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:30.040
Just calm down, everyone!

00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:34.790
Is that good enough?

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:36.120
No.

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:39.010
This is your punishment for leaving 
me behind to go on a vacation

00:04:39.010 --> 00:04:40.950
to the southern islands.

00:04:40.950 --> 00:04:43.670
You don't get to stop until I'm satisfied.

00:04:44.530 --> 00:04:45.740
Hibiki.

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:47.800
I'm here for your morning service.

00:04:48.210 --> 00:04:50.270
K-K-Kiriyume?!

00:04:50.270 --> 00:04:51.680
You again?

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:55.390
You barge in every day, 
and now you're in my bath!

00:04:55.390 --> 00:04:57.330
What do you think you're doing?

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:59.910
What's so wrong about a wife 
coming to her husband's house?

00:04:59.910 --> 00:05:01.070
You sister-in-law wannabe.

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:04.180
Stop getting between my and 
Hibiki's newlywed life.

00:05:04.180 --> 00:05:05.490
Who are you calling a sister-in-law?

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:08.710
How did you even get in, anyway?

00:05:08.710 --> 00:05:10.950
Through Hibiki's window.

00:05:11.550 --> 00:05:13.440
Th-That's trespassing.

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:14.710
You stalker!

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:16.270
What else can I do?

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:18.260
Hibiki won't give me a matching key.

00:05:18.260 --> 00:05:19.940
Just go home already!

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:22.500
Or I'll send you back to the 
island in a courier package!

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:24.370
How dare you?!

00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:36.140
Did something bad happen, Nukui-san?

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:38.060
No, nothing.

00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:39.650
R-Really?

00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:42.980
Thank you.

00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:49.210
Aigae-san.

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:51.780
Nukui-kun.

00:05:53.230 --> 00:05:54.290
You're lost?

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:55.290
Yes.

00:05:55.290 --> 00:05:59.790
We rented a room on the second 
floor of a shop around here.

00:05:59.790 --> 00:06:04.300
I went to the bookstore, 
and now I can't find my way home.

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:08.310
I couldn't even find the shoujo 
manga I was looking for.

00:06:08.310 --> 00:06:10.150
I'm so sad.

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:13.390
You like manga, huh, Aigae-san?

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:14.490
Yes.

00:06:14.490 --> 00:06:16.860
I saw a special about Akihabara on TV.

00:06:16.860 --> 00:06:19.190
There were shops full of manga.

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:21.770
I've always envied it.

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:25.030
Wow!

00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:28.830
There're houses everywhere, 
no matter how far we go.

00:06:28.830 --> 00:06:30.780
We're almost to Akihabara.

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:34.490
Sorry for making you take me there.

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:36.790
It's a river!

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:37.660
It's a river!

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:38.830
A bridge!

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:40.670
It's huge!

00:06:44.580 --> 00:06:48.050
I never knew so many humans existed.

00:06:49.450 --> 00:06:52.680
Look, maids in their natural habitat!

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:54.680
I've never seen them before.

00:06:55.980 --> 00:06:59.810
This whole building sells manga and anime?

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:01.800
I can't believe it.

00:07:01.800 --> 00:07:05.360
I'm sure you'll find the manga 
you're looking for here.

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:06.440
Yes.

00:07:06.970 --> 00:07:08.780
A-Are you okay?

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:09.950
Can you breathe?

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:12.640
Yes, I'm fine.

00:07:12.640 --> 00:07:15.280
This isn't something you'd get 
to experience on the island.

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:21.790
<i>I-I might not be okay with this.</i>

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:26.310
So the manga's here, huh?

00:07:26.310 --> 00:07:28.420
Yeah, I'm pretty sure.

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:33.800
<b>I Picked Up 10 Yen</b>

00:07:35.740 --> 00:07:43.650
Nukui-kun, this is just a guess, but I 
don't think this is the manga that I know.

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:45.310
Y-Yeah.

00:07:45.820 --> 00:07:49.080
I don't think you'll find the manga 
you're looking for on this floor.

00:07:49.080 --> 00:07:52.200
Yes, that's what I suspect.

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:57.450
That's what I suspect, but there's 
something alluring about this place.

00:07:57.450 --> 00:07:58.780
Something intense.

00:07:59.310 --> 00:08:01.330
I-Intense how?

00:08:03.130 --> 00:08:09.710
If I'm not mistaken, this is about a 
man and a man becoming intimate, right?

00:08:09.710 --> 00:08:10.820
Yeah.

00:08:10.820 --> 00:08:12.050
I guess?

00:08:12.050 --> 00:08:17.810
That means I can read it once and 
enjoy two peoples' worth of romance.

00:08:17.810 --> 00:08:19.900
It's such a good deal!

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:22.270
<b>Akihabara Denkigai
Summer Festival</b>

00:08:22.270 --> 00:08:29.900
I thought it'd be a good deal, but it was 
more expensive than a shoujo manga volume.

00:08:30.450 --> 00:08:34.030
I'm glad you found the manga 
you were looking for, though.

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:35.480
You're right.

00:08:35.480 --> 00:08:38.780
And I got to come to Akihabara.

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:43.620
Are you tired, Aigae-san?

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:48.380
I'm fine, but I think I'm a bit 
overwhelmed by all the people.

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:52.250
Why don't we take a break at a shop, then?

00:08:52.250 --> 00:08:53.630
Okay.

00:08:53.630 --> 00:08:57.190
Akihabara's known for the maid cafés, right?

00:08:57.190 --> 00:08:59.010
Maid cafés, huh?

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:01.190
I've never been in one, either.

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:05.230
Is that a karaoke shop?

00:09:05.230 --> 00:09:07.260
You like karaoke?

00:09:07.260 --> 00:09:10.480
More like, I've kind of admired them.

00:09:11.070 --> 00:09:15.450
There was one machine on the island, 
at the snack bar that Tome-san ran.

00:09:15.450 --> 00:09:18.250
But they wouldn't let kids use it.

00:09:19.540 --> 00:09:21.470
Why don't we go here, then?

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:23.330
Really?

00:09:23.950 --> 00:09:24.750
Yeah.

00:09:26.410 --> 00:09:30.250
My dreams are coming true all at once.

00:10:16.650 --> 00:10:21.050
I'm so happy. I never imagined 
I could have such a fun day.

00:10:21.050 --> 00:10:26.210
I feel kind of bad that I was 
the only one singing at karaoke.

00:10:26.210 --> 00:10:28.940
That's because I asked for it.

00:10:29.540 --> 00:10:31.830
You looked so happy singing, too.

00:10:31.830 --> 00:10:33.860
I wanted to keep listening.

00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:35.210
Nah.

00:10:35.210 --> 00:10:37.860
I just like singing.

00:10:39.340 --> 00:10:40.740
I can make it from here.

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:43.740
I know my way home from here.

00:10:43.740 --> 00:10:44.460
It's fine.

00:10:44.460 --> 00:10:46.130
I'll walk you to the shop.

00:10:46.130 --> 00:10:49.000
No, I don't want to give 
you any more trouble.

00:10:49.950 --> 00:10:50.750
But...

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:56.880
Besides, it'll be far from where 
you live if you walked me there.

00:10:57.910 --> 00:10:58.900
All right.

00:10:59.380 --> 00:11:01.260
Okay, let's say bye here.

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:03.080
I had fun.

00:11:03.080 --> 00:11:05.260
Our secret date.

00:11:07.110 --> 00:11:09.770
I'm getting embarrassed, 
now that I've said it out loud.

00:11:09.770 --> 00:11:11.730
Pardon me.

00:11:17.890 --> 00:11:22.400
Kyo, you understand why you're being 
forced to sit seiza style, don't you?

00:11:22.400 --> 00:11:24.780
Koume-chan told us.

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:30.620
You took Yuzuha-chan into a small room 
and enjoyed making all kinds of requests.

00:11:30.620 --> 00:11:32.230
N-No...

00:11:32.230 --> 00:11:34.950
It sounds wrong when you put it that way.

00:11:36.710 --> 00:11:39.460
Kyo-nii, are you a horndog?

00:11:39.460 --> 00:11:42.410
Hibiki, try saying my name.

00:11:42.410 --> 00:11:44.410
The name of your true wife.

00:11:44.410 --> 00:11:46.140
I-I'm single.

00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:47.940
Silence!

00:11:47.940 --> 00:11:51.480
Do you think you're going 
to BS your way out of this?

00:11:52.310 --> 00:11:53.950
Now, now, everyone.

00:11:53.950 --> 00:11:57.230
Nukui-kun did it for me out of kindness.

00:11:57.230 --> 00:11:58.980
You stay out of this, Yuzuha!

00:11:58.980 --> 00:12:01.060
G-Guys, hang on.

00:12:01.060 --> 00:12:03.090
That wasn't a date.

00:12:03.090 --> 00:12:06.740
Kyo, tell us what you did yesterday.

00:12:07.140 --> 00:12:08.020
Um...

00:12:08.020 --> 00:12:10.300
We went to Akihabara together,

00:12:10.300 --> 00:12:12.910
we went shopping, 
and then we went to karaoke.

00:12:13.360 --> 00:12:14.790
That <i>is</i> a date!

00:12:15.910 --> 00:12:18.920
Aigae-san, are you okay with this?

00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:21.300
Kiriyume seems to have the wrong idea.

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:22.890
It's all right.

00:12:22.890 --> 00:12:25.310
Rivalry is a given when you're in love.

00:12:25.310 --> 00:12:30.060
Kiryu-sama will become even more 
passionate if there's more drama.

00:12:31.530 --> 00:12:36.730
Yuzuha, it seems that you need to 
be disciplined before Hibiki does.

00:12:36.730 --> 00:12:37.720
Huh?

00:12:37.720 --> 00:12:39.110
Come over here!

00:12:38.270 --> 00:12:39.110
Oh, no!

00:12:39.550 --> 00:12:40.390
Kiryu-sama!

00:12:40.390 --> 00:12:43.400
Am I wrong about something?

00:12:43.400 --> 00:12:45.020
Everything!

00:12:45.020 --> 00:12:48.330
Hibiki, I'm not done talking to you yet.

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:51.040
I'm going to interrogate you lots later.

00:12:54.210 --> 00:12:56.370
So it <i>was</i> a date.

00:12:56.370 --> 00:12:58.750
Are you trying to win every route?

00:12:58.750 --> 00:13:00.540
N-No, I'm not!

00:13:00.540 --> 00:13:04.420
Aigae-san was apparently lost, so...

00:13:06.380 --> 00:13:09.260
Oh, so that's what happened.

00:13:09.260 --> 00:13:13.060
I guess I can believe it. 
You're such a Mr. Nice Guy.

00:13:14.540 --> 00:13:16.850
Helping is important.

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:20.210
So you understand.

00:13:20.210 --> 00:13:21.040
Yes.

00:13:21.040 --> 00:13:22.750
So you're going to have to go on...

00:13:23.600 --> 00:13:25.770
a d-date with us, too.

00:13:27.620 --> 00:13:30.940
Did you want to go on a 
date with Kyo-nii, too?

00:13:30.940 --> 00:13:32.660
N-No!

00:13:32.660 --> 00:13:36.220
I-It's not like I want to go 
on a date with Kyo or anything.

00:13:36.220 --> 00:13:40.290
But it's not fair that he'd 
go on a date just with Yuzuha.

00:13:40.290 --> 00:13:42.450
F-Fine.

00:13:42.450 --> 00:13:44.310
Then let's all go together, the four of us.

00:13:44.310 --> 00:13:45.900
Not the four of us.

00:13:46.830 --> 00:13:49.370
You went alone with Yuzuha.

00:13:49.370 --> 00:13:52.890
It won't be fair if you don't 
go with each of us individually.

00:13:56.770 --> 00:13:59.270
Rock, paper, scissors.

00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:01.520
Try again.

00:14:02.750 --> 00:14:03.940
Yay!

00:14:03.940 --> 00:14:05.030
I did it!

00:14:04.260 --> 00:14:05.030
Inconceivable.

00:14:05.430 --> 00:14:07.710
I'm first, Kyo-san.

00:14:10.430 --> 00:14:14.120
This turned out weird.

00:14:14.120 --> 00:14:16.290
K-Kyo-san.

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:18.210
Sorry to make you wait.

00:14:18.210 --> 00:14:21.030
Nah, I just got here, too.

00:14:22.570 --> 00:14:24.340
I'm glad.

00:14:24.770 --> 00:14:26.730
You look good in that.

00:14:27.880 --> 00:14:30.930
Apparently this is called 
my special occasion clothes.

00:14:32.190 --> 00:14:35.520
And underneath, I'm wearing 
my special occasion panties.

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:39.020
Th-That's too much information.

00:14:41.900 --> 00:14:42.490
Huh?

00:14:42.490 --> 00:14:43.930
Aren't you going to sit?

00:14:43.930 --> 00:14:46.070
N-No, I'll sit.

00:14:46.540 --> 00:14:48.030
Pardon me.

00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:56.690
Kyo-san, I'm not too heavy, am I?

00:14:56.690 --> 00:15:00.170
No, you're not heavy, but...

00:15:01.670 --> 00:15:02.810
What's that?

00:15:02.810 --> 00:15:03.550
Hush.

00:15:03.550 --> 00:15:05.690
This is what dating is, huh?

00:15:05.690 --> 00:15:07.920
I'm getting antsy.

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:08.920
Uh...

00:15:08.920 --> 00:15:09.990
Um...

00:15:15.540 --> 00:15:16.970
Kyo-san,

00:15:17.400 --> 00:15:18.970
I don't really know much about dating,

00:15:18.970 --> 00:15:22.230
but I'm going to do my best to 
make sure it's a proper date.

00:15:23.990 --> 00:15:24.890
Sure.

00:15:26.110 --> 00:15:27.890
<i>Think about something else.</i>

00:15:27.890 --> 00:15:29.630
<i>Distract yourself.</i>

00:15:29.630 --> 00:15:33.240
<i>Play some intense music in your head...</i>

00:15:33.240 --> 00:15:34.990
<i>And...</i>

00:15:46.540 --> 00:15:50.300
<b>Shinjiku Station</b>

00:15:47.830 --> 00:15:50.300
Let's lock arms, Kyo-san.

00:15:50.300 --> 00:15:52.000
O-Okay.

00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:53.310
If that's okay with you.

00:15:55.950 --> 00:15:58.440
This might be a bit hard.

00:15:58.440 --> 00:16:00.270
It might.

00:16:02.060 --> 00:16:05.930
Am I not good enough to be your partner?

00:16:09.390 --> 00:16:12.070
We might not be able to lock 
arms, but we can do this.

00:16:16.740 --> 00:16:19.380
Thank you, Kyo-san.

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:28.930
But why did you decide to come here?

00:16:28.930 --> 00:16:32.160
I want some stimulation.

00:16:32.160 --> 00:16:33.260
Stimulation?

00:16:33.260 --> 00:16:35.510
<b>Kabukicho Ichibangai</b>

00:16:36.710 --> 00:16:41.520
We have to do a research assignment 
for our summer homework.

00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:44.600
I couldn't decide what to do.

00:16:44.600 --> 00:16:49.770
So I thought I might be able to find 
some hints if I went somewhere lively.

00:16:50.090 --> 00:16:51.810
I see.

00:16:50.690 --> 00:16:52.650
<b>Except bicycles</b>

00:16:55.030 --> 00:17:00.260
We've been everywhere, and I 
still can't think of anything.

00:17:00.260 --> 00:17:04.160
Am I stupid?

00:17:04.160 --> 00:17:05.790
No, you're not.

00:17:05.790 --> 00:17:07.130
But...

00:17:07.130 --> 00:17:08.500
I know.

00:17:08.500 --> 00:17:11.920
How about a change of perspective, then?

00:17:11.920 --> 00:17:15.050
A change of perspective?

00:17:15.050 --> 00:17:16.240
Yeah.

00:17:16.240 --> 00:17:18.680
Let's see...

00:17:20.010 --> 00:17:25.230
How about you pretend you're someone 
completely different, and look around.

00:17:25.770 --> 00:17:29.060
You might discover something new that way.

00:17:29.990 --> 00:17:31.390
Okay.

00:17:31.390 --> 00:17:33.260
I'll try it.

00:17:33.770 --> 00:17:36.940
I'm going to pretend I'm 
someone completely different.

00:17:37.450 --> 00:17:39.070
Pretend...

00:17:39.070 --> 00:17:40.860
Pretend...

00:17:45.170 --> 00:17:46.460
Jun?

00:17:48.270 --> 00:17:50.650
We're going shopping, Kyo-sa—

00:17:52.020 --> 00:17:52.790
Kyo.

00:17:55.850 --> 00:17:57.210
Uh...

00:17:57.210 --> 00:17:59.900
What does... that mean?

00:18:00.590 --> 00:18:02.460
I'm an evil queen.

00:18:03.350 --> 00:18:07.060
She showed up in a Sunday morning anime.

00:18:07.060 --> 00:18:09.310
Is that no good?

00:18:09.310 --> 00:18:12.560
No, I think it's good.

00:18:12.560 --> 00:18:15.830
That's definitely different 
from your usual self.

00:18:15.830 --> 00:18:17.990
Let's give that a try.

00:18:19.420 --> 00:18:20.740
Okay.

00:18:25.150 --> 00:18:27.870
Kyo, we're going into this store.

00:18:27.870 --> 00:18:29.870
As you wish.

00:18:31.130 --> 00:18:33.630
Er... This store...

00:18:33.990 --> 00:18:38.270
My queen, why are we in this store?

00:18:38.270 --> 00:18:42.700
Because these are an evil queen's clothes.

00:18:43.700 --> 00:18:44.600
Welcome.

00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:46.790
I'm here for my swimsuit.

00:18:46.790 --> 00:18:48.070
Um...

00:18:48.070 --> 00:18:49.070
What kind?

00:18:49.070 --> 00:18:51.760
Like the one that was on display up front.

00:18:51.760 --> 00:18:53.520
I'd like black.

00:18:53.520 --> 00:18:56.340
I-I think you're a bit young to wear black.

00:18:56.340 --> 00:18:57.970
I'd like black.

00:18:59.490 --> 00:19:02.990
<b>Fitting Rooms</b>

00:19:00.140 --> 00:19:02.990
This is the one that was on display.

00:19:02.990 --> 00:19:05.450
Thanks. I'll try it on.

00:19:05.450 --> 00:19:07.290
But the size...

00:19:09.090 --> 00:19:10.520
Is she your sister?

00:19:10.520 --> 00:19:12.880
No, I'm a queen.

00:19:15.380 --> 00:19:17.510
<b>Fitting Rooms</b>

00:19:15.380 --> 00:19:17.510
I put it on, Kyo.

00:19:18.980 --> 00:19:20.990
H-How is it?

00:19:20.990 --> 00:19:22.500
Um...

00:19:22.500 --> 00:19:24.700
I don't think it's your size.

00:19:25.490 --> 00:19:28.140
Th-That's not true.

00:19:28.140 --> 00:19:32.650
It's a sexy, grown-up swimsuit fit for me.

00:19:45.710 --> 00:19:49.330
Operation Evil Queen was a disaster.

00:19:49.950 --> 00:19:55.290
I don't think I'm good at anything.

00:19:55.290 --> 00:19:56.840
That's not true.

00:19:57.300 --> 00:20:03.340
You're good on the guitar, and the music 
you make is really important to me.

00:20:05.810 --> 00:20:07.280
Kyo-san...

00:20:07.280 --> 00:20:08.720
Thank you.

00:20:09.190 --> 00:20:14.980
Nothing makes me happier than when 
you say good things about my music.

00:20:16.310 --> 00:20:20.050
I couldn't find a subject 
for my research assignment,

00:20:20.050 --> 00:20:24.610
but I'm really glad we 
got to go out together.

00:20:24.610 --> 00:20:25.830
Me, too.

00:20:25.830 --> 00:20:30.490
I'm glad I got to tell you something 
I've always had on my mind.

00:22:33.870 --> 00:22:38.210
Hey, I can see your head, Nozomi.

00:22:38.210 --> 00:22:39.060
No way.

00:22:39.060 --> 00:22:40.140
Zomi.

00:22:40.810 --> 00:22:43.050
And what are you doing, Sakura?

00:22:43.050 --> 00:22:44.730
Y-You got the wrong idea!

00:22:44.730 --> 00:22:47.130
Jun said she was going on a date with you,

00:22:47.130 --> 00:22:50.260
so I was keeping an eye on you 
to make sure you didn't make any mistakes.

00:22:50.260 --> 00:22:53.140
You really don't trust me.

00:22:53.140 --> 00:22:56.820
Well, you know, just to be safe.

00:22:56.820 --> 00:22:58.220
Sorry.

00:22:58.220 --> 00:23:00.520
You all came to watch, huh?

00:23:00.520 --> 00:23:04.810
You were worried about me and whether or 
not I could properly go on a date, right?

00:23:06.330 --> 00:23:10.150
All right, let's all have 
some donuts on our way home.

00:23:11.290 --> 00:23:14.160
Following people makes 
me surprisingly hungry.

00:23:14.160 --> 00:23:16.160
Is that all right, Jun?

00:23:18.250 --> 00:23:19.020
Yes.

00:23:21.230 --> 00:23:24.960
<b>Totally a Date</b>

00:23:25.450 --> 00:23:33.020
I've caused pandemonium by going 
on a date-ish outing with Aigae-san.

00:23:25.820 --> 00:23:41.500
<b>#11: Band Battles and Melodies</b>

00:23:33.020 --> 00:23:36.950
Wait, is this something I need to repent for?

00:23:36.950 --> 00:23:38.680
Lucky pervert.

00:23:38.680 --> 00:23:39.930
I'm innocent!
